Alembic migrations for the Natives backend.

Common commands (run from the backend/ directory with your venv active and a
valid DATABASE_URL in .env):

  alembic upgrade head        # apply all migrations
  alembic downgrade -1        # roll back one migration
  alembic revision --autogenerate -m "describe change"   # new migration
  alembic current             # show current revision
  alembic history             # list revisions

The database URL is read from app settings (app/core/config.py) in env.py, so
you do not set sqlalchemy.url in alembic.ini.
